{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 117, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the edge-3 skip, removing edge 5 leaves only edge 4 feeding the output, crippling information flow."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where there was no edge yields a much larger gain than swapping an existing conv/pool for skip."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Cutting edge 0 kills node 1, so the loss is smaller when edge 4 (from node 1) is already absent."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is already none, removing edge 4 leaves only the skip on edge 3 reaching the output, collapsing capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2 absent, removing edge 1 disconnects node 2 and makes edge 5 dead."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 0 is none node 1 is zero, so edge 2 already carries nothing and removing it is nearly harmless."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the skip when edge 4 is absent leaves the output dependent on a single path, hurting accuracy more."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 5 absent, edge 4 is the only learnable path into the output, so upgrading it to a 3x3 conv matters more."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a skip with a conv gains less than replacing a weak avg_pool, since skip already preserves signal."}, {"edit_ed